From 8960499335a661c74a7a7f71aaeecbc341e48cd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:03:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Numbered jump strip for long playlists in their own order

A playlist sorted by position has no letters to jump by, so a long one could only
be paged through. Above one page of items, the playlist now shows a strip with a
chip per page (1, 51, 101, ...). Tapping a chip loads from that offset and scrolls
the listing to it, and paging continues from there.

The strip needs the playlist's length, so the view counts it alongside the first
page and passes it down as the listing total. The strip stays hidden for other
sorts (the A-Z strip covers name orders) and while a search narrows the list.
